Grossy's Vegan Vodka Sauce
  --Dan Pelosi (aka Grossy Pelosi)

8 tbsp olive oil
2 tbsp vegan butter
3 garlic cloves, grated
1/2 tsp red pepper flakes (optional)
6 tbsp tomato paste
16 oz (2 c) cashew or coconut cream or coconut milk
6 tbsp vodka
2 boxes Banza Cascatelli (1 lb)
grated vegan parmesan cheese, for serving

Over medium heat, melt vegan butter, red pepper flakes (optional), and olive oil together in a saucepan. Add grated garlic and tomato paste. Whisk until fragrant. At the same time, boil Banza pasta in salty water, ~8-10 min. Whisk coconut or cashew cream into sauce for 5-6 min, until it darkens. Add vodka and whisk for another 5-6 min, until alcohol is cooked out. You will be able to smell the difference in the sauce. Drain pasta and rinse, reserving 1 c of pasta water. Add 1/2 c of your pasta water to the sawce and whisk until inappropriately thick. Sauce may take up to 20 min to get thick enough, and it is absolutely worth the wait. Add pasta to sauce and stir until coated and glossy. Serve with grated vegan parmesan or pecorino and enjoy!





Notes: if you don't want to use vodka, just skip, don't sub. can sub more olive oil for vegan butter. If you are using gluten-free pasta that is not made from chickpeas, add 1/2 tsp of cornstarch to the 1 c of pasta water you reserve. This will give you pasta water the starch it needs to make your sawce thick. If you want to add vegetables to your pasta, I recommend cooking vegetables separately and serving it alongside or on top of the pasta. Do not cook the vegetables in the sauce.
